# Proxy BlogSphere API calls to the Netlify Functions backend.
# Cloudflare Pages serves only static files from this repo, so /api/*
# is forwarded (200 = proxy, not redirect) to the live Netlify functions.
# This keeps posts, comments, contact and health working on Pages deploys.
/api/health https://blogggsphere.netlify.app/.netlify/functions/api-health 200
/api/public-data https://blogggsphere.netlify.app/.netlify/functions/api-public-data 200
/api/comments https://blogggsphere.netlify.app/.netlify/functions/api-comments 200
/api/contact https://blogggsphere.netlify.app/.netlify/functions/api-contact 200
# Also proxy the admin's Netlify-function calls (/.netlify/functions/* returns
# 404 on Pages today, so the admin cannot save posts either).
/.netlify/functions/* https://blogggsphere.netlify.app/.netlify/functions/:splat 200
